* Three-channel, 4 x 6L6 head (Dual / Triple Rectifier style) power amp: the 12AX7 long-tailed phase inverter (V5A, V5B) with its
* negative feedback network (47k, 0.1u and the presence shaping), four 6L6GC as two parallel pairs on fixed bias, the output
* transformer, and the HV supply with the node C filter. B+ (node a) is the rectifier / reservoir, integrated by the engine.
* It is the same family of circuit as the other 4 x 6L6 amp, with the values of this drawing (B+ 475 V, bias -52 V, 1k5 grid
* stoppers, 1k screen resistors, 82k / 91k phase inverter loads with 120p across them, node C through 2k7).
*
* Assumptions where the drawing is silent or ambiguous (change them here, not in code):
*  - feedback: the 8 ohm tap drives 47k and 0.1u into the phase inverter's 4.7k node; the resonance network of the other amp
*    is not there, the presence control shapes the feedback like in that amp (the drawing's per-channel presence is replaced by one);
*  - output transformer: 2.2k plate-to-plate onto the 8 ohm tap, 6 H per primary half, 40 ohm per half;
*  - bias: -52 V behind 3k with 10u, near 40 mA per tube with the stock 6L6GC;
*  - the Slave Level, the cross-coupling 75p and the standby switch are left out (standby closed);
*  - the supply: silicon rectifier, node C (V2B..V5) from B+ through 2k7 with 10u, RPREAMP stands for what the preamp draws from it.

S VAUDIO pin 32k 0
S VHT a 1 475
S VBIAS cb 3k -52
C C41 cb 0 10u

* V3 rail: 4.7k from B+, 47u, and the preamp's load (V2 / V1 stages are inside the preamp netlist).
R R59 a x 2k7
C C36 x 0 10u
R RPREAMP x 0 33k

* Phase inverter. P (pp) is the input node: the 0.022u (C49) is in the preamp (stage 3), so a large coupling cap here only sets the DC of the grid network; 100k to V4B's grid, 1M to the cathode
* node kk. V4A's grid sits behind 0.047u on node na (4.7k to ground, the feedback node) and 1M to kk.
C CIN pin pp 10u
R R48 pp gb 100k
R R50 pp kk 1M
R R53 kk ga 1M
R R51 kk na 10k
R R52 kk kc 470
R R57 na 0 4k7
C C31 na ga 47n
T V4B gb pb kc 12AX7
T V4A ga pa kc 12AX7
R R46 x pb 82k
C C120B x pb 120p
R R58 x pa 91k
C C120A x pa 120p

* Negative feedback and its resonance / presence shaping (t8 is the 8 ohm tap).
R R56 t8 na 47k
C C30 na nb 0.1u
C C8 nb pr 0.1u
R VR9_T pr wp 5k
R VR9_B wp 0 5k
C C62 nb wp 33n

* Output stage: 0.047u couplings, 220k grid returns to the bias, 2.2k stoppers (two tubes per half),
* 100p to ground.
C C29 pb pga 47n
C C28 pa pgb 47n
R R55 pga cb 220k
R R54 pgb cb 220k
R R206 pga g1 1k5/2
R R202 pgb g2 1k5/2
C C202 pga 0 100p
C C201 pgb 0 100p
P V5 g1 pt s1 0 6L6GCDS 2
P V6 g2 pbm s2 0 6L6GCDS 2
R R207 a s1 1k/2
R R203 a s2 1k/2

* Output transformer T2: primary halves around the B+ centre tap, one secondary for the 8 ohm tap.
R DCR_PT pt npt 40
R DCR_PB pbm npb 40
.param n8 = 2*1/sqrt(2200/8)
* Core saturation: SAT is the flux (volt-seconds) where the extra magnetising current equals the linear one; ~full-power
* plate-to-plate swing / (2 pi f), with f about 28-30 Hz for the large Marshall / Soldano / Peavey / Fender cores, 50 to 65 Hz for the small AC30 / tweed cores.
.xfmr OT L=6 SAT=4.4
  W npt a 1 pri
  W a npb 1 pri
  W t8 0 n8 sec
  K pri pri 0.9998
  K pri sec 0.9993
.end
R RLOAD t8 0 8
